    answerType: "single",
    explanation: "Offline approaches such as carrying portable drives to an AWS Data Transfer Terminal or using an AWS Partner offline data transfer service move tens of terabytes without depending on a limited or unreliable network link. AWS Snowball Edge, the former AWS offline option, stopped accepting new customers on November 7, 2025, and Snowball support ends on December 31, 2026, so AWS now points new customers to Data Transfer Terminal, AWS DataSync, or partner solutions, though the exam may still describe Snowball as the offline option.",
