    explanation: "A change set, including the drift-aware type that also compares against live resource state, previews how proposed template or parameter changes will affect the running stack, listing each resource action (Add, Modify, Remove) and whether a modification requires replacement, before you choose to execute it.",
    optionRationale: {
      a: "Change sets are the CloudFormation mechanism for reviewing the impact of an update before it is applied.",
      b: "Outputs export values from a stack; they do not preview changes.",
      c: "Nested stacks organize templates into reusable components but do not preview updates.",
      d: "Termination protection prevents the whole stack from being deleted; it does not show what an update will change.",
      e: "Drift detection compares a stack's actual resources with its template after deployment; it does not preview an upcoming update.",
      f: "A stack policy blocks updates to protected resources but does not show what an update would change.",
      g: "StackSets deploys stacks to multiple accounts and Regions; it does not preview resource-level changes.",
      h: "Rollback triggers monitor CloudWatch alarms during an update and roll back on breach; they do not show the planned changes beforehand.",
      i: "A drift-aware change set previews an update against both the template and the live resource state, listing every resource that will be added, modified, or replaced before anything is executed.",
    },
    referenceUrl: "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-cfn-updating-stacks-changesets.html",
