    correctOptionIds: ["a", "i"],
    answerType: "single",
    explanation: "User data is a script or cloud-init directive you pass when launching an instance. It runs automatically with root privileges during the first boot, making it the standard way to bootstrap instances by installing packages, downloading code, and configuring agents. Launch templates and Auto Scaling groups can include user data so every instance is configured identically.",
