    text: "A financial analytics application runs on EC2 instances in a single Availability Zone and reads millions of small objects per hour from Amazon S3. Even the latency of S3 Standard, which is tens of milliseconds, slows the job noticeably. The company wants a purpose-built S3 storage class that offers consistent single-digit millisecond data access for latency-sensitive workloads. Which option should it choose?",
