    id: "tech176",
    domain: "cloud-technology-and-services",
    text: "A security team wants to capture information about the IP traffic that is accepted and rejected at the network interfaces in a VPC, so that it can troubleshoot why an application cannot reach a database and analyze traffic patterns. The captured records should be delivered to Amazon CloudWatch Logs or Amazon S3. Which VPC feature provides this?",
    options: [
      { id: "a", text: "VPC Flow Logs" },
      { id: "b", text: "AWS CloudTrail" },
      { id: "c", text: "VPC Reachability Analyzer" },
      { id: "d", text: "Amazon CloudWatch metrics" },
      { id: "e", text: "AWS Network Firewall logs" },
      { id: "f", text: "VPC Traffic Mirroring" },
      { id: "g", text: "AWS Config configuration items" },
      { id: "h", text: "Amazon GuardDuty findings" },
      { id: "i", text: "Flow logs on a VPC, subnet, or network interface" },
    ],
    correctOptionIds: ["a", "i"],
    answerType: "single",
    explanation: "VPC Flow Logs capture metadata about IP traffic going to and from network interfaces in a VPC, including source and destination addresses, ports, protocol, and whether the traffic was accepted or rejected. Flow logs can be created at the VPC, subnet, or network interface level and published to CloudWatch Logs, Amazon S3, or Amazon Data Firehose.",
    optionRationale: {
      a: "Flow Logs record accepted and rejected traffic at network interfaces and deliver the records to CloudWatch Logs or S3.",
      b: "CloudTrail records API calls made in the account, such as who created a security group; it does not capture network packets or flows.",
      c: "Reachability Analyzer performs static configuration analysis to tell you whether a path is possible; it does not record actual traffic.",
      d: "CloudWatch metrics report aggregate statistics such as bytes in and out; they do not list individual connections or reject reasons.",
      e: "Network Firewall logs only traffic passing through a firewall endpoint, not all interface traffic accepted or rejected by security groups and NACLs.",
      f: "Traffic Mirroring copies full packets to an appliance for deep inspection; it does not produce accept/reject metadata records in CloudWatch Logs or S3.",
      g: "AWS Config records resource configuration history; it does not capture network traffic.",
      h: "GuardDuty analyzes flow logs for threats and produces findings; it does not deliver raw traffic records for troubleshooting.",
      i: "Flow logs can be created for a whole VPC, a subnet, or one network interface, and each records accepted and rejected traffic to CloudWatch Logs or S3.",
    },
    referenceUrl: "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/flow-logs.html",
    referenceLabel: "Logging IP traffic using VPC Flow Logs",
    consoleUrl: "https://console.aws.amazon.com/vpcconsole/home#vpcs:",
    consoleLabel: "VPC > Your VPCs > Flow logs",
