    explanation: "Route 53 Resolver is the DNS server built into every VPC. Resolver endpoints extend it across a hybrid network: an inbound endpoint gives on-premises DNS servers IP addresses inside the VPC to which they can forward queries for private hosted zones, and an outbound endpoint plus forwarding rules lets the VPC forward queries for on-premises domains to the corporate DNS servers over the VPN or Direct Connect connection.",
