    correctOptionIds: ["a", "i"],
    answerType: "single",
    explanation: "CloudWatch Synthetics lets you create canaries: configurable scripts (Node.js or Python, using headless Chromium) that run on a schedule to monitor endpoints and multi-step user flows such as login or checkout, even when there is no real user traffic. Canaries record success rate, duration, screenshots, and HAR files, publish metrics to CloudWatch, and can trigger alarms. Route 53 health checks can only test whether an endpoint responds, not whether a multi-step browser flow works.",
